@startuml stand_up
title scripts/up.sh: bringing the stand up

skinparam wrapWidth 220

start
if (Docker sees the card through CDI?) then (no)
  :Say why, and offer scripts/up.sh --cpu; <<#fff3cd>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Read the judge's model from config.yaml;
if (compose will create or start vllm?) then (yes)
  :Unload ollama's models, so vLLM finds the card free;
else (no: a warm stand)
endif
:docker compose up -d;

fork
  :postgresql;
  :dbmate: migrations;
  :seed: engines, prompts, the question bank,
MCP integrations, the code's sources;
fork again
  :ollama;
fork again
  :ollama-cpu;
fork again
  :vllm takes the card first;
  note right
    The first start downloads the weights.
  end note
end fork

partition "bootstrap, once every service above is healthy" {
  :vllm put to sleep, unless a job holds the card;
  :model rows from config, roles seated,
  vLLM rows filled from what it serves;
  :ollama reconciled: a missing model queues a pull,
  the repetition penalty is written in;
  :a corpus indexed only if the database holds none
  (an empty variant beside others is only logged),
  missing vector indexes built;
  :questions without a vector queued;
}

fork
  :rag-lab: the API;
fork again
  :repos-owner hands the volume to the host's user;
  :worker: the job queue;
fork again
  :by profile: vllm-embed, vllm-rerank, vllm-cpu,
converter-docling and converter-mineru (convert);
note right
  A converter answers /health from its supervisor
  with the tool not running: the tool starts only
  when a job takes the card, so healthy is not held.
end note
end fork
stop
@enduml
